window.MC_CONTENT_EXTRA.push({"a":"jayce","b":"locke","win":["Jayce","Jayce","Jayce","Jayce","Skill","Locke","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Levels 1-4","text":"Max poke phase — Shock Blast chunks him for free; zone him off everything."},{"when":"Enemy 6 + first item","text":"His execute-plus-burst window — stay above threshold and poke from max range only."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Safe poke rebalances the lane — chunk, disengage, repeat."}],"wants":{"you":["Free poke leads levels 1-4","Zero fights inside his engage range","Him chunked before Soul Ignition heals"],"foe":["Weathered poke into 6 plus item","Purgatory grounding your leap","Forced close-range all-ins"]},"early":"The first four stages are a shooting gallery: the Q-E accelerated Shock Blast zones him off the wave, and Ashen Pursuit — his only way in — is a flat 10s. Step up in the ten seconds after he blinks, not before. Dodge Ritual Nails at 950; its marks are what his autos cash in. Chunk him at every reset, deny CS, and stack plates.","mid":"Level 6 changes the stakes — your ult is a stance swap while Purgatory grounds, slows and executes from 1000 range. Grounded, To the Skies! is gone and so is your escape, which is why the Gate is the disengage that still works. Silver Stake grows with your missing health, so chip compounds: 60% is not half-safe.","late":"Two-plus items the lane settles into an even, winnable dance: safe poke against burst, and whoever respects ranges wins. Soul Ignition is his tell — it costs him health up front and heals a portion back only at the END of its duration, so burst him inside it and have Grievous Wounds already bought. He needs a caught Jayce.","whys":["Level 1 is Jayce — you out-range him completely and poke with zero risk.","Level 2 stays yours: the Q-E combo zones him off the wave entirely.","Level 3 is Jayce — ranged Shock Blast keeps chunking him and he simply cannot reach you.","Levels 4-5 stay yours — the poke advantage persists while he still lacks a burst spike.","Even at 6: your ult is a stance swap, while Purgatory grounds To the Skies! away and executes from 1000.","Locke's — Purgatory plus item burst is a genuine all-in kill, and Silver Stake hits harder the lower you already are.","2+ items reverts to skill — your safe poke offsets his burst threat, and whoever plays their range better wins."]});
