window.MC_CONTENT_EXTRA.push({"a":"jayce","b":"zaahen","win":["Skill","Jayce","Jayce","Skill","Skill","Jayce","Jayce"],"spikes":[{"when":"Levels 2-3","text":"Aureate Rush arrives — poke only with an exit planned and Thundering Blow up."},{"when":"Levels 4-5","text":"Gate spacing resets the lane — your best farming stretch."},{"when":"Enemy first item","text":"Bruiser stats plus Aureate Rush into Grim Deliverance — max range or nothing."}],"wants":{"you":["Poke behind pre-placed escape gates","Thundering Blow his Aureate Rush","Wins by rotation, not duels"],"foe":["Aureate Rush onto squishy cannon form","Rush into a Grim Deliverance","Isolated side-lane brawls late"]},"early":"Respect his levels 2-3 � Aureate Rush comes online and every greedy walk-up becomes his trade on your cannon form. The Darkin Glaive auto-resets and heals him, so the auto wind-up is your tell and Grievous Wounds is the answer. Poke off gate speed with an exit planned, hold Thundering Blow to punt him off, and reach the 4-5 stretch.","mid":"From 6 the math is blunt: if his all-in lands, nothing in your kit answers Grim Deliverance — so it must never land. At his first item, Aureate Rush into that ultimate can one-shot you, and the dash deals percent max health, so raw HP is not the fix. Knock him back and expect Dreaded Return to drag you straight back. Play maximum range, gate every trade, and shove-rotate.","late":"Two-plus items his bruiser body beats you in any side-lane duel, so make the game about everything else: poke sieges, cross-map rotations, and teamfights where gate-accelerated Shock Blasts chunk him before he ever reaches contact. Knock him back off every engage, kite behind your frontline, and let range beat rage for the rest of the game.","whys":["Level 1 is neutral — auto trades only, and he has no gap-close online yet.","Level 2 is Zaahen's: his gap-close threat arrives, and your poke attempts get punished on the approach.","Level 3 stays his — he closes onto your squishy cannon form and converts your poke windows into his trades.","Levels 4-5 even out — Acceleration Gate poke lets you hold distance and reset the spacing war.","Level 6 stays even — if his all-in lands your kit has no answer to the ult, but landing it through your gate speed and spacing is the hard part.","First item is Zaahen's — bruiser stats shrug your poke and his E-into-R can one-shot you; range discipline is life.","2+ items stays his — a scaled Zaahen's bruiser body wins the side lane even from even, so out-rotate instead of dueling."]});
