window.MC_CONTENT_EXTRA.push({"a":"jayce","b":"masteryi","win":["Jayce","Jayce","Jayce","Skill","Skill","Master Yi","Master Yi"],"spikes":[{"when":"Levels 1-3","text":"Artillery phase — deny CS, chunk every walk-up, build the lead."},{"when":"Enemy first item","text":"Alpha Strike untargetability plus his first item — poke range only."},{"when":"Enemy 2+ items","text":"Wuju Style true damage crushes you up close — peel with the hammer knockback."}],"wants":{"you":["A starved Yi levels 1-3","Leads cashed into plates and roams","Late poke sieges, never duels"],"foe":["Survival through the artillery phase","First-item all-in run-downs","Late true-damage side-lane duels"]},"early":"Own the artillery phase completely — Shock Blast through Acceleration Gate keeps Yi off CS at levels 1-2, and Thundering Blow answers the rare all-in at 3. Alpha Strike is 20s at rank 1 and he is untargetable through the whole dash, so fire the orb after it lands, never into it. Every missed minion delays his items, and his items are the entire matchup.","mid":"You get no ult spike at 6 while he gets Highlander — 85s, and it makes him immune to slows, so your Shock Blast slow stops kiting him. Convert before his first item: plates off your shove, roams off gate speed, and picks with your jungler. When he is on the map, poke from maximum range and punt him away with the hammer the instant he closes.","late":"Two-plus items his true damage crushes a squishy Jayce in any duel, so your late game is played at 1500 range: siege with accelerated Shock Blasts, chunk him before fights start, and hold hammer E as the anti-Highlander peel — slow immunity leaves displacement as your only answer, and it also ends a Meditate channel. Buy Grievous Wounds, stay with your team.","whys":["Level 1 is Jayce — ranged Shock Blast poke dominates while he has nothing to answer with.","Level 2 stays yours: gate-empowered artillery keeps him off CS completely.","Level 3 is Jayce — poke plus the hammer knockback still out-trades everything he tries.","Levels 4-5 even out as his scaling starts — the free window is closing.","Level 6 stays skill — no ult spike for you, and an 85s Highlander alone does not yet break your spacing.","First item is Master Yi's — his spike lets him gap-close and win, so stop taking contested fights.","2+ items stays Yi — true-damage DPS crushes a squishy Jayce, so win with poke and picks, never duels."]});
